{"semantic_chronology":{"public_id":{"uuids":["9955bdbe-64a8-4f5a-a9b7-b748977bd890"]},"referenced_component_public_id":{"uuids":["8d5831a5-7ede-53fa-b3e7-e5c43151c5e3"]},"pattern_for_semantic_public_id":{"uuids":["3734fb0a-4c14-5831-9a61-4743af609e7a"]},"semantic_versions":[{"stamp_chronology_public_id":{"uuids":["23b1b371-02fa-5035-aed0-63a71582a2ea"]},"fields":[{"string_value":"A new Test Performed record was added in the Device Extension Module. It lists SARS-CoV-2 as the analyte, with the N, E and RdRP gene targets, and anterior nares swab as the specimen. Its test is a qualitative SARS-CoV-2 nucleic acid amplification test (concept 3e20aec1-f1ea-55c9-af23-d6cabf79ca6c). It names four GeneXpert Dx System instruments (GXXVI-16, GXXVI-4, GXXVI-8 and GXIV-2), and its example UCUM units are \"Not applicable\".\n\nI couldn't confirm which concept the record is attached to. The record's UUID didn't resolve as a concept, and the tools didn't show the link back to a parent concept. The device concept GeneXpert® XPRS-COV2-10, a child of Respiratory Specimen Nucleic Acid Sars-Cov-2 Test, is the likely subject, but that is my inference."}]}]}}
